                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d0e424e8-7781-3ea7-a039-c9452af91d0e",
                        "entry_id": "3fe3555f-e1b0-35a1-a289-e415f8a41a0e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "iemand met veel ervaring"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "10651418-44dc-4a9d-aca8-3fe6869665e0",
                                "sense_id": "d0e424e8-7781-3ea7-a039-c9452af91d0e",
                                "text": "Sparta, de enige ploeg zonder punten uit de laatste drie duels, zou wellicht Michel Breuer op kunnen stellen om de Rotterdamse hoop meer leven in te blazen. Geen enkele speler in de eredivisie won zo vaak (6) van Ajax als de 37-jarige routinier."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "13ff5cdc-64fb-33ea-817e-44f8f1eb80c8",
                        "entry_id": "3fe3555f-e1b0-35a1-a289-e415f8a41a0e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "iemand die zonder aandacht en interesse zijn werk volledig automatisch afraffelt, iemand die bekend is met alle (vuile) trucjes van het vak"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "pejorative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "623f8ae4-dfc1-4834-8611-4a39724c600b",
                                "sense_id": "13ff5cdc-64fb-33ea-817e-44f8f1eb80c8",
                                "text": "Aan het woord is een lid van de raad van bestuur, dat liever anoniem blijft. Een routinier wel, die het leven op de universiteit door en door kent. Gevraagd naar de machinaties van de academische macht doet hij met plezier een boekje open."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fa512adc-cbe0-407f-b615-cb9798cbc5f6",
                        "source_entry_id": "3fe3555f-e1b0-35a1-a289-e415f8a41a0e",
                        "source_sense_id": "d0e424e8-7781-3ea7-a039-c9452af91d0e",
                        "source_sense_description": "iemand met veel ervaring",
                        "target_lang_word": "routineer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "routineer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71ab38b7-67ed-39e3-96c4-b98bce5f5bb3",
                                        "entry_id": "83b735c0-1447-3174-9718-e99d4bfb4995",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who follows routine rather than innovating."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d25572e4-596f-47e9-804b-28ff81108afe",
                                                "sense_id": "71ab38b7-67ed-39e3-96c4-b98bce5f5bb3",
                                                "text": "As a routineer you will fill in the details of other men's concepts."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "884b42a0-c9fb-4431-b19f-246495793536",
                                                "sense_id": "71ab38b7-67ed-39e3-96c4-b98bce5f5bb3",
                                                "text": "The ladder was so designed that the docile, the efficient routineers, those who knew how to please their superiors, ascended more easily than the strong-minded, the clever, and the efficient."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "feeef585-fb2f-4d4d-a23f-d40f35ffdea8",
                                                "sense_id": "71ab38b7-67ed-39e3-96c4-b98bce5f5bb3",
                                                "text": "Affidavit practice usually initially involves analyzing the skill level and/or qualifications of the affiant, which should be of the routineer in the art. When an affiant's skill level is higher than that required by the routineer for a particular application, an examiner may callenge the affidavit since it would not be made by a routineer in the art, and therefore would not be probative as to the amount of experimentation required by a routineer in the art to implement the invention."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e807eec-395a-458d-8d06-272238464cb2",
                                                "sense_id": "71ab38b7-67ed-39e3-96c4-b98bce5f5bb3",
                                                "text": "The routineers, Lippmann maintained, had used “the sterile tyranny of the taboo\" to smother impulses, when they should have recognized that \"every lust is capable of some civilized impression.\" Instead of channeling desire in the right direction, the routineer forbade it; he had fought against the emerging trusts back in the 1880s and he now was fighting against the emerging unions."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
